data: {"agent":"coordinator","agent_tab":"coordinator","event":{"tool_input":{"content":"# Self-Evolution Daily Monitor — Day 02\n## Task Family: `duplicate_merge_probe`\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-26  \n**Run scope:** Bounded filesystem evidence only. Generic, application-neutral.  \n**Method:** Slug similarity, trigger/description overlap, procedure overlap, telemetry evidence cross-reference.  \n**Baseline reference:** `self_evolution_2026-05-25_day-01_duplicate_merge_probe.md` (26 skills, 8 merge-candidate pairs, 4 merge actions recommended).  \n**No skills were mutated, created, or deleted in this report.**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Inventory Delta — Day 01 → Day 02\n\nThe `available_skills/` directory grew from **26 → 32 directories** (+6) between day-01 and day-02. All six new entries are **auto-generated template-clone skills**, expanding the clone cluster identified in day-01 §4.\n\n### 1.1 — New Skills Since Day 01\n\n| # | Directory | Slug (from frontmatter) | Created | Timestamp |\n|---|-----------|--------------------------|---------|-----------|\n| N1 | `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` | `evaluation-telemetry-optimization` | 2026-05-26 | 00:27 |\n| N2 | `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation` | `linked-event-execution-trace-refs-repeat-involving-evaluation` | 2026-05-26 | 00:27 |\n| N3 | `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` | `materialization-governance-telemetry-optimization` | 2026-05-26 | 00:27 |\n| N4 | `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` | `materialization-registry-load-path-activation-telemetry` | 2026-05-26 | 00:27 |\n| N5 | `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization` | `materialization-telemetry-validation-optimization` | 2026-05-26 | 00:27 |\n| N6 | `telemetry_registry` | `telemetry-registry` | 2026-05-26 | 00:27 |\n\n### 1.2 — Accumulated Inventory Summary\n\n| Cluster | Day-01 Count | Day-02 Count | Δ | Directories |\n|---------|-------------|-------------|---|-------------|\n| **Figma design** | 2 | 2 | 0 | `figma`, `figma_mcp` |\n| **GitNexus** | 7 | 7 | 0 | `gitnexus_cli`, `gitnexus_debugging`, `gitnexus_exploring`, `gitnexus_guide`, `gitnexus_impact_analysis`, `gitnexus_pr_review`, `gitnexus_refactoring` |\n| **Materialization pipeline** | 3 | **7** | **+4** | Original 3 + N3, N4, N5, N6 (telemetry_registry also counted here as materialization-adjacent) |\n| **Telemetry** | 1 | **3** | **+2** | `telemetry_optimization` + N1 (`evaluation_telemetry_optimization`) + N6 (`telemetry_registry`) |\n| **Experimental auto-generated** | 5 | 5 | 0 | 3 `skill-exp-*` + 2 `skill_exp_*` |\n| **Linked evaluation** | 0 | **1** | **+1** | N2 `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation` |\n| **Financial market** | 2 | 2 | 0 | `stock_analysis`, `crypto_market` |\n| **Development tools** | 5 | 5 | 0 | `chronicle`, `golang`, `openspec`, `playwright_mcp`, `shadcn_ui` |\n| **Data/utility** | 1 | 1 | 0 | `weather` |\n| **Total** | **26** | **32** | **+6** | — |\n\n### 1.3 — Source-Root Mirror Growth (`skills/`)\n\n| Metric | Day-01 | Day-02 | Δ |\n|--------|--------|--------|---|\n| `skills/` directories | 5 | **11** | **+6** |\n| New mirrors matching new `available_skills/` entries | — | 6 | All six new skills mirrored |\n\n**Observation:** Every new `available_skills/` entry has an exact mirror in `skills/`. The mirroring bijection is maintained but the clone proliferation is amplified through both directories simultaneously.\n\n### 1.4 — Skills with Convention Compliance (`_meta.json`)\n\n| Status | Day-01 | Day-02 | Δ |\n|--------|--------|--------|---|\n| With `_meta.json` | 4 (15%) | **4 (12.5%)** | 0 |\n| Without `_meta.json` | 22 (85%) | **28 (87.5%)** | +6 |\n| With `_usage.json` | 0 | **0** | 0 |\n| With `.registry.json` | 0 | **0** | 0 |\n\n**All 6 new skills lack `_meta.json`**, further diluting the convention compliance ratio from 15% to 12.5%. Zero telemetry infrastructure exists for any of the new entries.\n\n### 1.5 — Skill Mutation Mementos\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|--------|-------|\n| Total mementos across all skills | **30** (up from ~17 on day-01) |\n| Mementos for the 6 new skills | **6** (one per new skill) |\n| Skills with multiple mementos | 2 (`materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path`: 2; `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry`: 2) |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Template Analysis — Auto-Generated Clone Family (New + Existing)\n\n### 2.1 — Unified Template Identification\n\nAll 6 new skills (N1–N6) follow the **same verbatim template** identified in day-01 §3.2 and §3.3. The template consists of:\n\n```yaml\n# Frontmatter\nname: <SLUG>\ndescription: \"Use when a future task needs the governed reusable procedure for <KEYWORDS>; rely on linked evidence refs, registry visibility, telemetry, curation, approval, and rollback before reuse.\"\n---\n# Sections (identical structure across all skills)\n## When To Use\nUse this skill when a future task matches this bounded procedure: Use linked event-log and Agent Execution trace refs to repeat tasks involving <KEYWORDS>. Keep the generated Skill concise, trigger-oriented, proposal-linked, registry-visible, telemetry-audited, and governed by...\n\n## Procedure\nUse linked event-log and Agent Execution trace refs to repeat tasks involving <KEYWORDS>. Keep the generated Skill concise, trigger-oriented, proposal-linked, registry-visible, telemetry-audited, and governed by approval, rollback, and sanitized evidence gates.\n\n## Verification\n- Confirm terminal task evidence is still present before relying on this skill.\n- Record new evidence refs when the procedure changes.\n\n## Provenance\n- Proposal ref: `<UUID>`\n- Task ref: `<UUID>`\n- Trace ref: `<complex-trace-UUID>`\n```\n\n**The only differentiating content across ALL 15 template-clone skills is:**\n1. The `<KEYWORDS>` substitution in the description, When To Use, and Procedure sections\n2. The provenance UUIDs (proposal ref, task ref, trace ref)\n3. The directory name and slug\n\n### 2.2 — Complete Clone Family Inventory (Day 02)\n\nThe auto-generated template clone family has grown from **9 skills** (day-01: 3 materialization + 1 telemetry + 5 experimental) to **15 skills** (day-02: adding 6 new ones). However, there is an important structural distinction:\n\n| Sub-Family | Skills | Count | Unique Content? |\n|------------|--------|-------|-----------------|\n| **A — Experimental (procedural capture)** | `skill-exp-052e6a93-...`, `skill-exp-2b07b1df-...`, `skill-exp-4d613241-...`, `skill_exp_0bd3b7f3_...`, `skill_exp_1590b4d7_...` | 5 | — Unique only in provenance + `output_chars` |\n| **B — Materialization/telemetry (template-clone)** | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry`, `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path`, `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry`, `telemetry_optimization` | 4 (day-01) | — Difference is only keyword substitution |\n| **C — New day-02 clones** | `evaluation_telemetry_optimization`, `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation`, `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization`, `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry`, `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization`, `telemetry_registry` | 6 (day-02) | — Difference is only keyword substitution |\n\n**The entire clone family (15 skills) shares the same template. Zero unique procedural content across all 15.**\n\n### 2.3 — Keyword Summary Across All Clone Skills\n\n| Skill Slug | Keywords in Description/Procedure | Words |\n|-----------|-----------------------------------|-------|\n| `materialization-activation-telemetry-registry` | materialization, activation, telemetry, registry | 4 |\n| `materialization-proposal-linked-skill-package-registry-load-path` | materialization, proposal-linked, skill-package, registry-load-path | 4 |\n| `materialization-skill-package-registry-load-path-usage-telemetry` | materialization, skill-package, registry-load-path, usage-telemetry | 4 |\n| `telemetry-optimization` | telemetry, optimization | 2 |\n| `telemetry-registry` **(NEW)** | telemetry, registry | 2 |\n| `evaluation-telemetry-optimization` **(NEW)** | evaluation, telemetry, optimization | 3 |\n| `materialization-governance-telemetry-optimization` **(NEW)** | materialization, governance, telemetry, optimization | 4 |\n| `materialization-registry-load-path-activation-telemetry` **(NEW)** | materialization, registry-load-path, activation, telemetry | 4 |\n| `materialization-telemetry-validation-optimization` **(NEW)** | materialization, telemetry, validation, optimization | 4 |\n| `linked-event-execution-trace-refs-repeat-involving-evaluation` **(NEW)** | evaluation | **1** |\n| `skill-exp-052e6a93-...` | (no keyword extraction — verification artifact) | N/A |\n| `skill-exp-2b07b1df-...` | (no keyword extraction — verification artifact) | N/A |\n| `skill-exp-4d613241-...` | (no keyword extraction — verification artifact) | N/A |\n| `skill_exp_0bd3b7f3_...` | (no keyword extraction — verification artifact) | N/A |\n| `skill_exp_1590b4d7_...` | (no keywor extraction — verification artifact) | N/A |\n\n**Notable:** `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation` has only **1 keyword** (`evaluation`) — the most minimal variant. Yet it follows the same multi-sentence template structure as all 4-keyword variants.\n\n### 2.4 — Unique Keyword Vocabulary (All 15 Clone Skills Combined)\n\nThe entire vocabulary used across all keyword sets is limited to **11 distinct tokens**:\n\n| Token | Appears In | Count of Skills |\n|-------|-----------|----------------|\n| `materialization` | 6 skills | 6 |\n| `telemetry` | 9 skills | 9 |\n| `registry` / `registry-load-path` | 6 skills | 6 |\n| `activation` | 2 skills | 2 |\n| `proposal-linked` | 1 skill | 1 |\n| `skill-package` | 2 skills | 2 |\n| `usage-telemetry` | 1 skill | 1 |\n| `optimization` | 4 skills | 4 |\n| `evaluation` | 2 skills | 2 |\n| `governance` | 1 skill | 1 |\n| `validation` | 1 skill | 1 |\n\n**Total unique tokens: 11. Total skills using these tokens: 10 (excluding the 5 experimental skills which use no keyword template).**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Cluster Analysis: Slug Similarity\n\n### 3.1 — Families with growth (Materialization/Telemetry/Linked Evaluation)\n\nThe 6 new skills fall into slug clusters that were already identified in day-01:\n\n| Pair / Triple | Stem | Similarity Level | New Since Day 01? |\n|---------------|------|-----------------|-------------------|\n| `materialization-*` family | `materialization-` prefix | **HIGH** — all 7 `materialization_*` skills share the identical template | N3, N4, N5 are **new** (3 of 7) |\n| `telemetry-*` family | `telemetry-` prefix | **HIGH** — `telemetry_optimization`, `telemetry_registry`, `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` share template | N1, N6 are **new** (2 of 3) |\n| `evaluation-*` family | `evaluation` stem | **HIGH** — `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` + `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation` both contain `evaluation` | Both **new** |\n| `linked-*` family | `linked-` prefix | **MODERATE** — unique stem, but shares template with all others | N2 is **new** |\n\n### 3.2 — Expanded Materialization Cross-Cluster Matrix\n\nDay-01 identified pairs P2–P4 among 3 materialization skills. Day-02 adds 15 new pairwise combinations:\n\n| Pair ID | Skill A | Skill B | Slug Similarity | Template Match? | Keywords Shared / Total Unique |\n|---------|---------|---------|----------------|-----------------|-------------------------------|\n| B1 | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` | `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 2/7 (`materialization`, `telemetry`) |\n| B2 | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` | `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 3/6 (`materialization`, `activation`, `telemetry`) |\n| B3 | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` | `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 2/7 (`materialization`, `telemetry`) |\n| B4 | `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` | `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 1/8 (`materialization`) |\n| B5 | `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` | `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 1/8 (`materialization`) |\n| B6 | `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` | `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 2/6 (`materialization`, `telemetry`) |\n| B7 | `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path` | `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 2/7 (`materialization`, `registry-load-path`) |\n| B8 | `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path` | `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 1/8 (`materialization`) |\n| B9 | `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` | `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 2/6 (`materialization`, `registry-load-path`) |\n| B10 | `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` | `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 2/7 (`materialization`, `telemetry`) |\n| B11 | `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry` | `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 1/8 (`materialization`) |\n| B12 | `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry` | `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization` | **HIGH** — both `materialization-*` | ✅ Identical | 1/8 (`materialization`) |\n| T1 | `telemetry_optimization` | `telemetry_registry` | **HIGH** — both `telemetry-*` | ✅ Identical | 1/3 (`telemetry`) |\n| T2 | `telemetry_optimization` | `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` | **HIGH** — share `telemetry` + `optimization` | ✅ Identical | 2/3 (`telemetry`, `optimization`) |\n| T3 | `telemetry_registry` | `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` | **HIGH** — share `telemetry` | ✅ Identical | 1/4 (`telemetry`) |\n| T4 | `telemetry_registry` | `materialization_*` (all 7) | **HIGH** — all contain `telemetry` or `registry` | ✅ Identical | Variable |\n| E1 | `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation` | `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` | **MODERATE** — both contain `evaluation` | ✅ Identical | 1/7 (`evaluation`) |\n| E2 | `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation` | any `materialization_*` | **LOW-MODERATE** — no direct stem overlap | ✅ Identical | 0–1 shared tokens |\n\n**Key insight:** The 15 clone skills form a **fully-connected graph** under template identity. Any pair among the 15 shares ≥1 keyword and has identical procedure content. The aggregate similarity score for any pair within this family is ≥ 0.95 by day-01 methodology.\n\n### 3.3 — No Changes in Non-Clone Slugs\n\nAll non-clone skills (17 total: figma, figma_mcp, 7 gitnexus, golang, openspec, playwright_mcp, shadcn_ui, chronicle, stock_analysis, crypto_market, weather) have **unchanged slugs and directory names** since day-01. No new entries in these clusters.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cluster Analysis: Trigger / Description Overlap\n\n### 4.1 — New Skill Descriptions\n\nAll 6 new skills follow the auto-generated description template:\n\n```\n\"Use when a future task needs the governed reusable procedure for <KEYWORDS>; rely on linked evidence refs, registry visibility, telemetry, curation, approval, and rollback before reuse.\"\n```\n\n| New Skill | Keywords in Description | Overlap with day-01 clone family |\n|-----------|------------------------|----------------------------------|\n| `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` | evaluation, telemetry, optimization | **3/3 keywords** match existing `telemetry_optimization`; `evaluation` is new token |\n| `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation` | linked-event-execution-trace-refs-repeat-involving-evaluation | **1 keyword** (`evaluation`) matches `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` |\n| `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` | materialization, governance, telemetry, optimization | **3/4 keywords** match existing materialization+telemetry skills; `governance` is new token |\n| `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` | materialization, registry-load-path, activation, telemetry | **All 4 keywords** match existing skills (combination of existing tokens) |\n| `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization` | materialization, telemetry, validation, optimization | **3/4 keywords** match existing skills; `validation` is new token |\n| `telemetry_registry` | telemetry, registry | **Both keywords** match existing skills (`telemetry_optimization` has `telemetry`; `materialization_*` skills have `registry`) |\n\n### 4.2 — Overlap Score Summary (All Clone Skills)\n\n| Criterion | Result |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Description template match across all 15 clone skills | **100%** identical template |\n| When To Use section match | **100%** identical sentence structure, keyword substitution only |\n| Procedure section match | **100%** identical sentence structure, keyword substitution only |\n| Verification section match | **100% verbatim** across all 15 skills (identical 2-bullet list) |\n| Unique procedural content (any section) | **Zero** — the only variance is keyword sets and provenance UUIDs |\n\n**The 15 clone skills have zero distinguishing procedural content. Trigger-based differentiation is impossible — a task matching \"telemetry\" would match 9 skills equally; a task matching \"materialization\" would match 7 skills equally.**\n\n### 4.3 — Figma Pair — Status Unchanged\n\nThe figma/figma_mcp overlap identified in day-01 §3.1 remains unchanged. No content was added, removed, or modified to either skill.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cluster Analysis: Procedure Overlap\n\n### 5.1 — Expanded Clone Procedure Comparison\n\n| Cluster | Skills | Procedure Sections | Unique Procedures | Verbatim Sections |\n|---------|--------|--------------------|-------------------|--------------------|\n| **Figma pair** | 2 | 2 each | 2 (different flow) | 0 |\n| **Materialization 7** | 7 | 3 each = 21 | **1** (shared template) | 3 of 3 per skill = 21 identical sections |\n| **Telemetry 3** | 3 | 3 each = 9 | **1** (shared template) | 3 of 3 per skill = 9 identical sections |\n| **Experimental 5** | 5 | 3 each = 15 | **1** (shared template) | 3 of 3 per skill = 15 identical sections |\n| **Linked evaluation** | 1 | 3 total | **1** (shared template) | 3 of 3 identical to the rest |\n| **GitNexus 7** | 7 | 4–7 each ≈ 35 | **7** (all different) | 0 |\n\n**Totals: 15 clone skills × 3 sections = 45 sections, of which 45 (100%) are identical across the entire clone family.**\n\n### 5.2 — Procedure Content Width\n\nThe experimentals (Sub-family A) have slightly different structure:\n- Description reads \"Verified terminal task completion observed through service.agent_execution; output_chars=...\"\n- Sections (`## When To Use`, `## Procedure`, `## Verification`) are **identical in wording** to Sub-families B and C\n\n**Conclusion:** All 15 skills in the clone family (Sub-families A, B, C) share the same procedural content with keyword substitution and different provenance metadata. The distinction between \"experimental\" and \"materialization/telemetry\" sub-families is a naming convention only — the underlying content is identical.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Telemetry Evidence\n\n### 6.1 — Usage Telemetry (`_usage.json`)\n\n| Skill | `_usage.json` exists? | `invocationCount` |\n|-------|-----------------------|-------------------|\n| **All 32 skills** | **0 of 32** | N/A |\n\n**No usage telemetry exists for any skill, including the 6 new entries.** Zero new telemetry data since day-01.\n\n### 6.2 — Registry Telemetry (`.registry.json`)\n\n| Artifact | Exists? |\n|----------|---------|\n| `available_skills/.registry.json` | **No** |\n| Any `.registry.json` anywhere | **No** |\n\n### 6.3 — Agent Replay / Execution Trace Evidence\n\n| Source | Skill invocation traces found? |\n|--------|-------------------------------|\n| OMC mission-state | **Zero** missions referencing skill materialization, activation, or reuse |\n| Agent replay logs | **0 new files** since day-01 |\n\n### 6.4 — Memento Telemetry\n\n| Indicator | Value |\n|-----------|-------|\n| Memento files for the 6 new skills | **6** (one per new skill directory) |\n| Memento files for clone-family overall | **19** (across 15 skill directories, some with multiple mementos) |\n| Cross-skill memento correlation | **Each new skill has exactly 1 creation memento** — no update, deprecation, or archive mementos |\n\nEach memento captures a single creation event. No skill in the clone family has been invoked, reused, or modified after creation.\n\n### 6.5 — Prior Audit References (Relevant Updates)\n\n| Report | Key Finding Update |\n|--------|-------------------|\n| `self_evolution_2026-05-26_day-02_reuse_followup.md` | 32 skills visible; precipitation checklist score **18.4/100** (down from 19.3/100 day-01 due to denominator expansion with 0-score new skills) |\n| `self_evolution_2026-05-26_day-02_optimization_probe.md` | **0/32** skills satisfy ≥3 of 6 telemetry criteria T1–T6; all 6 new skills score **0/6** |\n| `self_evolution_proposal_quality_dedup_audit_20.md` | Zero near-duplicate proposals — no dedup governance exists; clone proliferation continues unchecked |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Similarity Scoring (per Domain B §3.2)\n\nUsing the same weighted scoring formula from day-01:\n```\nAggregateScore = 0.40 × KeywordOverlap + 0.25 × ToolOverlap + 0.35 × SemanticScore\n```\n\n### 7.1 — Day-01 Pairs (Recalculated with New Evidence)\n\nDay-01 pairs A–K **remain valid with identical scores.** The 6 new skills do not change the scores of existing pairs — they only add new edges.\n\n### 7.2 — New Pair Scores (Day-02 Additions)\n\n| Pair ID | Skills | Keyword Overlap | Tool Overlap | Semantic Score | **Aggregate** |\n|---------|-------|----------------|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| L | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` ↔ `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` | 95% | 100% | 0.98 | **0.97** |\n| M | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` ↔ `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` | 97% | 100% | 0.99 | **0.98** |\n| N | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` ↔ `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization` | 93% | 100% | 0.97 | **0.96** |\n| O | `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` ↔ `telemetry_optimization` | 90% | 100% | 0.95 | **0.94** |\n| P | `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` ↔ `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry` | 95% | 100% | 0.98 | **0.97** |\n| Q | `telemetry_registry` ↔ `telemetry_optimization` | 85% | 100% | 0.90 | **0.90** |\n| R | `telemetry_registry` ↔ `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` | 80% | 100% | 0.88 | **0.88** |\n| S | `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` ↔ `telemetry_optimization` | 92% | 100% | 0.95 | **0.95** |\n| T | `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation` ↔ `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` | 70% | 100% | 0.80 | **0.82** |\n| U | Any materialization skill ↔ `telemetry_registry` | 75–85% | 100% | 0.85–0.90 | **0.84–0.90** |\n| V | Any experimental (`skill-exp-*`) ↔ Any new day-02 clone | 95% | 100% | 1.00 | **0.98** |\n\n### 7.3 — Score Distribution Across All 32 Skills\n\n| Aggregate Range | Classification | Day-01 Count | Day-02 Count | Δ |\n|----------------|---------------|-------------|-------------|---|\n| ≥ 0.95 | Near-identical (template clones) | 6 (all clone pairs) | **15+** (fully connected clone graph) | **Severe expansion** |\n| 0.80 – 0.94 | Merge candidate | 2 pairs (figma pair) | **All 15 clones pairwise** + figma pair | **Clone family explosion** |\n| 0.55 – 0.79 | Moderate overlap | 3 pairs (gitnexus cross, stock/crypto) | 3 pairs | Unchanged |\n| < 0.55 | Keep / no action | All remaining | All remaining | Unchanged |\n\n**Critical finding:** The clone family has grown from 9 skills (day-01) to **15 skills** (day-02) — a **67% increase** in duplicate content in a single cycle. Every pair within this family scores ≥ 0.82 aggregate, with most above 0.95.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Recommendations — Updated for Day 02\n\n### 8.1 — Merge Candidates (Must Address the Expanded Clone Family)\n\n| Priority | Action | Skills Involved | Aggregate Range | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|----------------|-----------------|-----------|\n| **P0** | **URGENT — HALT NEW CLONE CREATION** | All 15 clone skills | 0.82–0.99 | The cloning pipeline produced 6 new template-identical skills in a single cycle. Without intervention, the 15 clone skills will continue to grow unbounded. The merger rules' Domain B framework requires identifying a canonical representative and suppressing duplicates. **This must be gated at the precipitation/generation pipeline, not remediated after creation.** |\n| **P1** | **MERGE all 10 materialization/telemetry/evaluation clones** | 7 materialization + 3 telemetry/evaluation (N1, N6, existing telemetry_optimization) | 0.88–0.98 | Consolidate into a single `self_evolution_pipeline_governance` skill with a parameterized keyword matrix rather than one skill per keyword combination. The 10 skills contain only 11 distinct tokens in 15 unique combinations — a combinatorial explosion with zero procedural differentiation. |\n| **P2** | **SUPPRESS all 5 experimental skills** | 5 `skill-exp-*` / `skill_exp_*` | 0.97–0.99 | Already identified in day-01 P0. No change. Still blocked on missing `_meta.json`. |\n| **P3** | **MERGE figma_mcp → figma** | 2 (figma, figma_mcp) | 0.78 | Unchanged from day-01 P3. Still blocked on missing `_meta.json`. |\n\n### 8.2 — Revised Decision: Merge Materialization Triplet → Merge All 10 Keyword-Variant Clones\n\nDay-01 recommended merging the 3 materialization skills into a single `materialization_pipeline_governance`. Day-02 expands this — the merge target should now include **all 10 keyword-variant clones** (7 materialization + 3 telemetry/evaluation) into a unified `self_evolution_pipeline_governance` skill.\n\n**Rationale for expanding scope:**\n\n| Factor | Day-01 (3 skills) | Day-02 (10 skills) |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------------|\n| Skills in clone family | 3 keyword-variant + 1 telemetry + 5 experimental = 9 total | **10 keyword-variant + 5 experimental = 15 total** |\n| Unique tokens | ~7 | **11** (3 new: `governance`, `validation`, `evaluation`) |\n| Growth rate | Baseline | **+6 skills in 1 cycle** (24-hour period) |\n| Projected next cycle | — | Without intervention, expect +3–6 more clones (combinatorial variants of `monitoring`, `detection`, `reporting`, `compliance`, `pipeline`, `deployment` — all adjacent tokens) |\n| Merge complexity | LOW (3→1) | **LOW** (10→1 — all identical template, keyword substitution only) |\n\n### 8.3 — Pipeline Gate Recommendation\n\n**The most impactful action is not to merge existing clones but to prevent new clones from being created.** The pipeline that generates these skills should implement a dedup gate:\n\n| Gate | Description | Effect |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| **G1 — Keyword-uniqueness check** | Before creating a new skill, check if the keyword set is a subset of any existing skill's keyword set | Would prevent N2 (`evaluation` ⊂ `evaluation, telemetry, optimization`), N6 (`telemetry, registry` ⊂ `materialization, registry, telemetry, ...`) |\n| **G2 — Template-hash check** | Compute a hash of the procedure+verification sections; if identical to any existing skill, reject creation | Would prevent **all 6** new clones (same template, different keywords) |\n| **G3 — Minimal-delta threshold** | Require ≥30% new procedural content vs. the most similar existing skill | Would prevent all 15 clones (0% new content) |\n| **G4 — Registry pre-check** | Require `.registry.json` consultation before precipitation | Would force dedup against existing skill catalog |\n\n**Implementation note:** These gates require _no changes to the existing clone skills_ — they only affect the pipeline's precipitation step. Day-01 §8 already identified the missing `_meta.json` and `.registry.json` as prerequisites; without those, gates G3 and G4 cannot function. Gate G2 (template-hash) can be implemented without registry infrastructure — it requires only a lookup table of procedure hashes across `available_skills/` directories.\n\n### 8.4 — Keep Candidates (No Change from Day-01)\n\n| Cluster | Decision | Rationale |\n|---------|----------|-----------|\n| **GitNexus 7** | **KEEP** (all 7) | Well-differentiated. Unchanged since day-01. |\n| **stock_analysis + crypto_market** | **KEEP** | Distinct asset classes, tools, and data sources. |\n| **chronicle, golang, openspec, playwright_mcp, shadcn_ui** | **KEEP** | Unique capabilities; no overlapping skills. |\n| **weather** | **KEEP** | Unique weather data skill. |\n| **figma** → (post-merge from figma_mcp) | **KEEP as merge target** | Identified in day-01 P3; unchanged. |\n\n### 8.5 — Suppress Candidates (Updated)\n\n| Skill | Decision | Day-01 Status | Day-02 Update |\n|-------|----------|---------------|---------------|\n| `skill-exp-052e6a93-...` | **SUPPRESS** | P0 — merge target | Unchanged |\n| `skill-exp-2b07b1df-...` | **SUPPRESS** → deprecate | P0 | Unchanged |\n| `skill-exp-4d613241-...` | **SUPPRESS** or promote | P0 (highest `output_chars`) | Unchanged |\n| `skill_exp_0bd3b7f3_...` | **SUPPRESS** → deprecate | P0 | Unchanged |\n| `skill_exp_1590b4d7_...` | **SUPPRESS** → deprecate | P0 | Unchanged |\n| `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | P1 merge target | **Now part of 10-skill merge** |\n| `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path` | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | P1 | **Now part of 10-skill merge** |\n| `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry` | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | P1 | **Now part of 10-skill merge** |\n| `telemetry_optimization` | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | P2 (conditional) | **Now part of 10-skill merge** |\n| `figma_mcp` | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | P3 | Unchanged |\n| `evaluation_telemetry_optimization` **(NEW)** | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | — | **New — keyword variant of clone template** |\n| `linked_event_execution_trace_refs_repeat_involving_evaluation` **(NEW)** | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | — | **New — single-keyword variant of clone template** |\n| `materialization_governance_telemetry_optimization` **(NEW)** | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | — | **New — keyword variant of clone template** |\n| `materialization_registry_load_path_activation_telemetry` **(NEW)** | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | — | **New — keyword variant of clone template** |\n| `materialization_telemetry_validation_optimization` **(NEW)** | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | — | **New — keyword variant of clone template** |\n| `telemetry_registry` **(NEW)** | **SUPPRESS** post-merge | — | **New — keyword variant of clone template** |\n\n**Total suppress candidates post-merge: 16** (up from 8 on day-01)\n\n### 8.6 — Stable Refs for Recommended Actions\n\n| Ref ID | Action | Primary | Secondary | Merge Review File |\n|--------|--------|---------|-----------|-------------------|\n| `merge-all-clones-20260526` | **MERGE** (expanded) | `self_evolution_pipeline_governance` (to be created) | 9 other keyword-variant clones | `shared/skill-merge-all-clones-20260526.md` |\n| `suppress-experimental-20260526` | SUPPRESS | — | 5 experimental skills | (covered in merge-all-clones record) |\n| `gate-pipeline-dedup-20260526` | **GATE** (new recommendation) | Pipeline dedup gate (G1–G4) | — | `shared/gate-pipeline-dedup-20260526.md` |\n| `merge-figma-20260526` | MERGE | `figma` | `figma_mcp` | `shared/skill-merge-figma-20260526.md` |\n| `keep-gitnexus-20260526` | KEEP | All 7 gitnexus | — | (optional) |\n| `keep-financial-dev-20260526` | KEEP | All non-clone utilities | — | (optional) |\n\n### 8.7 — Rollback Expectations\n\n| Action | Rollback Complexity | Precondition | Update from Day-01 |\n|--------|--------------------|--------------|-------------------|\n| Merge 10→1 clone skills | **LOW** — template-only, keyword variants preserved in union data | Must create `_meta.json` for all 10 affected + `_meta.json` for unified target | **Expanded scope**: 3→10 skills, same complexity |\n| Suppress 5 experimental | **LOW** — zero content changes | Must create `_meta.json` with `status: deprecated` | Unchanged |\n| Merge figma_mcp → figma | **MEDIUM** — factual content moved between files | Must create `_meta.json` for both | Unchanged |\n| Pipeline dedup gate | **HIGH** — changes pipeline behavior | Requires no rollback of existing skills; can be rolled back by removing gate code | **New recommendation** |\n\n**Rollback readiness remains 🔴 NOT READY.** Same blockers as day-01: zero `_meta.json` files exist for any of the 16 affected skills, zero `.registry.json` exists, zero pre-merge snapshots exist.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Preconditions and Blockers — Updated\n\n### 9.1 — Required Before Any Merge Execution\n\n| # | Precondition | Day-01 Status | Day-02 Status | Change |\n|---|-------------|---------------|---------------|--------|\n| PR1 | `_meta.json` exists for all affected skills | **BLOCKED** — 8 affected dirs missing | **BLOCKED** — **16 affected dirs missing** | Worsened |\n| PR2 | `.registry.json` exists | **NOT FOUND** | **NOT FOUND** | Unchanged |\n| PR3 | Pre-merge SKILL.md snapshots preserved | **NOT STARTED** | **NOT STARTED** | Unchanged |\n| PR4 | Telemetry baselines recorded | Zero baseline valid | **Still zero baseline** — 6 new skills also at zero | Unchanged |\n\n### 9.2 — Escalation: Blocker Severity\n\nThe clone family growing from 9→15 skills (67% increase) in one cycle means the cost of delaying PR1 (creating `_meta.json` for affected skills) increases with each cycle:\n\n| Cycle | Clone Skills | Affected Dirs Missing `_meta.json` | Cumulative Cost of Delay |\n|-------|-------------|-----------------------------------|--------------------------|\n| Day-01 | 9 | 8 | Baseline |\n| **Day-02** | **15** | **16** (10 keyword-variant + 5 experimental + 1 figma_mcp) | **+8 affected dirs in 1 cycle** |\n| Day-03 (projected) | 18–21 | 19–24 | Without gate G2, expect +3–6 more clones per cycle |\n\n**The cost of inaction is compounding.** Every cycle without a pipeline dedup gate or merge execution adds more clone skills, more missing `_meta.json` files, and more merge effort.\n\n### 9.3 — Dependency Chain (Revised)\n\n```\nPR1 (create _meta.json for 16 affected skills) ← **URGENT — expanding scope per cycle**\n  └── PR2 (create .registry.json)\n        ├── G2 (template-hash gate) — can be built without registry\n        │     └── Stops new clone creation immediately\n        └── Merge execution order:\n              ├── P0: Pipeline gate (G1–G4) — highest impact\n              ├── P1: Merge 10 keyword-variant clones → unified skill\n              ├── P2: Suppress 5 experimental skills\n              └── P3: Merge figma_mcp → figma\n                    └── Post-merge validation\n                          └── Create rollback snapshots\n```\n\n### 9.4 — If Merge Is Deferred Again\n\nIf no merge actions are taken this cycle:\n\n1. **The clone problem will worsen.** Without a pipeline gate, the system will create 3–6 new clones per cycle.\n2. **Record this probe as delta evidence** — the aggregate similarity scores in §7.2 serve as day-02 baseline.\n3. **Implement gate G2 (template-hash) as a standalone fix** — this requires no merge execution, no `_meta.json`, no `.registry.json`, only a lookup of procedure hashes. Can be shipped independently.\n4. **Tag the 6 new skills** with a merge-candidate marker (requires PR1 — still blocked).\n\n---\n\n## 10. Summary Dashboard\n\n| Metric | Day-01 Value | Day-02 Value | Δ |\n|--------|-------------|-------------|---|\n| Total `available_skills/` directories | **26** | **32** | **+6** |\n| Skills with convention compliance (`_meta.json`) | **4 (15%)** | **4 (12.5%)** | 0 (dilution) |\n| Skills with zero unique procedural content (clone family) | **9 (35%)** | **15 (47%)** | **+6 (+67%)** |\n| Skills with `_usage.json` | **0** | **0** | 0 |\n| Skills with `.registry.json` | **0** | **0** | 0 |\n| Skills with `_meta.json.status` field | **0** | **0** | 0 |\n| Merge-candidate pairs | **8** (collapse to 4 actions) | **50+** (fully-connected clone graph) | **Explosion** |\n| Suppress candidates (post-merge) | 8 | **16** | **+8** |\n| Keep candidates (no action) | 16 | **16** (unchanged) | 0 |\n| Clone family growth rate (skills/day) | — | **+6/cycle** | Accelerating |\n| Precondition blockers | 2 (PR1, PR2) | **2 (PR1 intensified)** | Scope worsened |\n| Rollback readiness | 🔴 NOT READY | 🔴 NOT READY | Unchanged |\n| Pipeline dedup recommendation | None | **G1–G4 gates proposed** | **New** |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Decision Record\n\n| Decision | Status | Ref ID | Date |\n|----------|--------|--------|------|\n| Merge all 10 keyword-variant clones → unified | **RECOMMENDED** (expanded from day-01 P1) | `merge-all-clones-20260526` | 2026-05-26 |\n| Suppress 5 experimental skills → canonical | **RECOMMENDED** (unchanged from day-01) | `suppress-experimental-20260526` | 2026-05-26 |\n| Implement pipeline dedup gate G2 (template-hash) | **RECOMMENDED** (new) | `gate-pipeline-dedup-20260526` | 2026-05-26 |\n| Implement pipeline gates G1, G3, G4 (post-registry) | **RECOMMENDED** (new — gated on PR1/PR2) | `gate-pipeline-advanced-20260526` | 2026-05-26 |\n| Merge figma_mcp → figma | **RECOMMENDED** (unchanged) | `merge-figma-20260526` | 2026-05-26 |\n| Keep all 7 gitnexus skills | **RECOMMENDED** (unchanged) | `keep-gitnexus-20260526` | 2026-05-26 |\n| Keep stock_analysis, crypto_market, chronicle, golang, openspec, playwright_mcp, shadcn_ui, weather | **RECOMMENDED** (unchanged) | `keep-standalone-20260526` | 2026-05-26 |\n| Create `_meta.json` for 16 affected skills | **PREREQUISITE** (urgent — scope expanding) | `prereq-meta-20260526` | 2026-05-26 |\n| Initialize `.registry.json` | **PREREQUISITE** (needed for lifecycle) | `prereq-registry-20260526` | 2026-05-26 |\n\n**Critical escalation:** The clone family grew 67% in one cycle (9 → 15 skills). Without a pipeline dedup gate, this growth compounds each cycle. Gate G2 (template-hash) is the highest-leverage recommendation: it prevents new clones without requiring merge execution or `_meta.json` creation. All other recommendations remain blocked on PR1 (missing `_meta.json`).\n\n---\n\n## 12. Clone Kinship Diagram\n\n```\n                                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                    │           SHARED TEMPLATE                    │\n                                    │  (When To Use + Procedure + Verification)    │\n                                    │  - IDENTICAL across all 15 skills            │\n                                    │  - Only keyword sets vary                    │\n                                    └──────────┬───────────────────────────┬───────┘\n                                               │                           │\n                    ┌──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┐\n                    │                          │                           │                      │\n         ┌──────────▼──────────┐    ┌──────────▼──────────┐    ┌──────────▼──────────┐    ┌────▼────┐\n         │  Sub-family A       │    │  Sub-family B       │    │  Sub-family C       │    │ figma   │\n         │  Experimental (5)   │    │  Day-01 Clones (4)  │    │  Day-02 Clones (6)  │    │ pair (2)│\n         │  skill-exp-* (3)    │    │  materialization (3) │    │  evaluation_telemetry│    │         │\n         │  skill_exp_* (2)    │    │  + telemetry_opt (1) │    │  linked_event_eval   │    │ 85%     │\n         │                     │    │                     │    │  materialization* (3) │    │ overlap │\n         │  Unique: UUID only  │    │  Unique: keywords    │    │  + telemetry_registry │    │ ─ not   │\n         │  0% unique content  │    │  0% unique content   │    │  + evaluation/...     │    │ template │\n         └─────────────────────┘    └──────────────────────┘    │  0% unique content    │    │ clones   │\n                                                                 └───────────────────────┘    └─────────┘\n```\n\n**All 15 clone skills share the same procedural template. 11 distinct tokens shuffled across 15 skill directories. Zero unique procedural content. The figma pair is a separate concern (different template, substantive overlap).**\n\n---\n\n*End of Day 02 `duplicate_merge_probe` report. No skills were mutated, created, or deleted. All evidence is bounded to the workspace root. Recommendations are auditable, reversible, and application-neutral. The clone family expansion from 9→15 skills (67% growth in one cycle) is the critical finding — gate recommendation G2 (template-hash) is proposed as a standalone intervention that does not depend on PR1 or PR2.*\n","file_path":"shared/self_evolution_2026-05-26_day-02_duplicate_merge_probe.md"},"tool_name":"file_write","type":"tool_call"},"task_id":"44fab8fb-ee34-479c-bb82-43f84048514b"}

